        </div>
        <div className="mt-4 space-y-1.5 border-t border-white/[0.06] pt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">
          <p>
            A click is matched to a signup only when the account is created through the link itself (the newest unmatched
            click for that code is credited). A creator code typed into the checkout promo box, an admin attach, or a
            signup that predates click tracking has no click to match — so &ldquo;customers attached&rdquo; can be larger
            than &ldquo;clicks matched&rdquo;, and is not a click-through rate.
          </p>
          <p>
            &ldquo;New account&rdquo; means the account was created at most 24 hours before it was attached; anything
            older was an existing customer attached later.
          </p>
          {t.otherCodeClicks > 0 && (
            <p>
              {plural(t.otherCodeClicks, "other link click")} in this range carried a code that is no partner&apos;s
              (a peer refer-a-friend code, a typo, or a deleted partner) and {t.otherCodeClicks === 1 ? "is" : "are"} not
              counted.
            </p>
          )}
          {t.clicksTruncated && (
            <p className="text-amber-300">
              This range has more clicks than one page can read — click figures cover the first 200,000 only. Narrow
              the range for exact numbers.
